== Intelligent-agent / AI-agent identity audit ==

This is the principal ontology-risk boundary in Wave 8.

The corpus deliberately keeps two concepts:

<pre>
Intelligent agent
= established general computational abstraction

AI agent
= contemporary applied AI-system term
</pre>

[[Intelligent agent]] is grounded in classical Russell/Norvig/Wooldridge agent theory and can describe systems with no LLM, natural language, external tools, or modern foundation model.

[[AI agent]] is grounded in current 2024–2026 usage around AI-powered multi-step systems, often with models, tools, memory/state, planning, retrieval, and execution loops.

The article explicitly states that current “AI agent” / “agentic AI” taxonomy is not fully standardized.

[[AI agent]] is therefore assigned '''Supported''' rather than Established.

No duplicate semantic identity is created because the historical scope and implementation scope remain explicit.

